  "section_notes": "S1 requires 24-hour regulator reporting for all incidents and 48-hour customer/neighbour notice. S2 sets a 55°C test with a permanent 7% failure cap, owner and regulator access to results but no public publication. S3 mandates new-unit shut-off from adoption and a 72-month retrofit deadline with feasibility alternatives. S4 requires built-in suppression 36 months after adoption. S5 triggers regulator review and corrective-action planning above 8/100k, but recall is not automatic and notices are prompt."
